{"id": "EUVD-2026-86835", "enisaUuid": "876d9ace-adb4-3880-ae5e-67bd4561c515", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Serialize NVMe unsol ctx list with a per-fcport lock\n\nThe fcport->unsol_ctx_head list is modified from several contexts without\na common lock. Entries are added in qla2xxx_process_purls_iocb() from the\nresponse queue ISR (under the qpair qp_lock), while they are removed from\nqla2xxx_process_purls_pkt() (DPC/purex worker), qla_nvme_xmt_ls_rsp()\n(NVMe-FC transport callback) and qla_nvme_release_lsrsp_cmd_kref() (SRB\ncompletion). The qpair qp_lock cannot serialize this per-fcport list since\nmultiqueue adapters add entries through different qpairs, so a concurrent\nadd and delete (or two concurrent deletes) can corrupt the list pointers.\n\nIntroduce a dedicated per-fcport spinlock, unsol_ctx_lock, initialized in\nqla2x00_alloc_fcport(), and take it around every list_add_tail()/list_del()\non unsol_ctx_head. The add nests under the existing qp_lock; no delete path\ntakes qp_lock, so the lock order is consistent and deadlock free.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:02", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c71726cdfda93ae169a75c7b1697eb870303125", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1ee12eecbab9674fb73c9e00a93fac655d5a5dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b211d138cad86f749826d6132db6388eded992d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d8ad6bc8cc5eff1870cef00a0d611f38f8b6bd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76da0c43c63eb0496649e372ac64466364d0fe7d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rmg2-25hr-q94v", "CVE-2026-97527"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "219e7769-9633-3303-a55f-a3ac31ee570c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "286616fa-9d53-34b4-bfc3-62584d232e0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <b211d138cad86f749826d6132db6388eded992d8"}, {"id": "3ae66546-ff3a-3f64-b8a5-e816dbc7e46b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "6eb38d8f-90fa-3185-8470-229b0d21d3bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <6c71726cdfda93ae169a75c7b1697eb870303125"}, {"id": "96628a70-c488-3738-b3c8-9abcad861ab9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "9bebdb94-ee80-39cc-a063-9cc24d04a726", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <76da0c43c63eb0496649e372ac64466364d0fe7d"}, {"id": "aad188a4-7e27-320e-a4b3-a572e4284c62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b200759e-88aa-3903-9f77-41eceb4e6bd8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <4d8ad6bc8cc5eff1870cef00a0d611f38f8b6bd0"}, {"id": "b296d5cb-3877-3176-80f1-ea7c94ad95a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "d6dd0a56-d8b5-3aab-86e2-e53cb896be7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "e80e35b5-a414-3d30-b86f-00b03bbee9ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "efc59e4c-f7c8-388c-8779-a6463e233756", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <c1ee12eecbab9674fb73c9e00a93fac655d5a5dc"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4a179cbf-06b9-3623-a958-6d4e31fdeb9e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}